From 5c471dc289c944661da6ce8953c8a648f25151e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:55:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Round 5: Carry metrics as serialized JSON and render
 calendar metrics once

Domain evaluations now return metrics as serialized JSON (Box<RawValue>)
that records embed verbatim, instead of a serde_json::Value tree that is
serialized later. Calendar metrics depend only on the model, so they are
rendered once at preparation and copied into each full record. The CLI's
Value result parses the same text back, and a unit test checks that run()
equals the parsed batch output for every model kind, traced and untraced.

Rejected before this round: templating the SIR provenance documents
(serial, 1.02x), recorded in evidence/performance-0.3.0/rejected/.

Workload: domain2 (48 calendar cases with 350 segments, full records),
11 samples.
Before median: 2.653 ms. After median: 0.035 ms. Speedup: 76.78x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
